skill: "benefits-leave-administration"
sections[3]:
  - "# benefits-leave-administration\n\nAdminister benefits enrollment windows and leave accrual enforcement. Use at enrollment windows, when the provider export arrives each month, when an employee questions a balance, or when a policy exception is requested so exceptions are logged with approvals instead of absorbed silently.\n\nOwner: role-hr-ops-specialist (pod-people, people_ops). Direct human technical prose; zero conversational fluff.\n\n## Inputs and Outputs\n\nContract in TOON, as consumed by the runbook:\n\n```\nallowed_tools[4]:\n  - read_file\n  - write_file\n  - run_command\n  - ask_question\ninputs: \"benefits policy benefits-policy.toon; provider eligibility export; accrual ledger leave-ledger.toon; time-off requests queue\"\noutputs: \"agents/artifacts/people/benefits-register.toon with enrollment states and effective dates; leave-reconciliation.toon with drift report; leave-exception-log.toon\"\n```\n\nThe agent refuses to run with missing or stale inputs: it stops and emits an ask_question naming the missing file instead of inventing values.\n"
  - "## Workflow\n\n1. Load benefits-policy.toon and record its version; every computed balance in this cycle is valid against that version only.\n2. Reconcile provider eligibility against the internal roster; additions and removals are listed with effective dates, not merged silently.\n3. Compute accrual balances per employee from leave-ledger.toon and compare against the provider export; drift beyond 0.5 days is flagged with direction and cause class (policy, timing or data entry).\n4. Apply time-off policy rules to the request queue: notice period, blackout windows and concurrent-approval limits; approvals outside policy require an exception record.\n5. Log every approved exception in leave-exception-log.toon with approver, reason and expiry; an exception without an expiry is a permanent policy change and must be treated as one.\n6. For open enrollment windows, track completion per employee and chase at 50 percent and 90 percent of the window; emit ask_question for employees unreachable after both chases.\n7. Write benefits-register.toon and leave-reconciliation.toon; carry unresolved drift into the next cycle rather than forcing balances to match.\n"
  - "## Handoff\n\nexceptions visible to role-hr-ops lead; payroll deductions align with payroll-cycle-ops.\n"
